# Only the root target was listed. Git worktrees under .claude carry their own,
# and one of them measured 8.8 GB -- all of it sent to the daemon as build
# context on `docker build .` from the main checkout. Match every target, and
# exclude the agent/tooling state outright the way .gitignore already does.
/target
**/target
.claude
.git
.github
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
checkpoint.json
last-verified.json
**/*.pdb
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
# Grant drafts: contact details, budgets and an unlisted demo video. `docs/grant`
# was listed; `helios-bsc-grant` was not, so the build context carried ~80 MB of
# private material into every `docker build`. Neither belongs in an image layer
# or in a context sent to a daemon.
docs/grant
helios-bsc-grant
scripts/__pycache__
